WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:11.710
Mō tātou, a, mō ka uri a muri ake nei

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:17.290
Over the last couple of months, we’ve reached
some tremendous Regeneration milestones.

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:21.390
In June, the Minister for Greater Christchurch
Regeneration, the Honourable Megan Woods,

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:26.320
held an official ceremony for the handover
of Regeneration land into Council ownership.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:34.190
This is about land going back to local ownership
with communities being fully in power of the

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:38.250
future of what happens in their community
and I think that is something that everyone

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.990
in Canterbury will celebrate.

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:45.040
And $18.6 million dollars in funding over
the next 10 years has been approved for the

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:48.320
Regeneration by the Council in the recent
Long Term Plan

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:54.860
It’s excellent, it means the next 2-3 years
of projects are now firmly set in concrete.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:01:00.030
Finishing the Wharf here, and then moving
into the playing fields, and bmx track and

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:01.030
dog park.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:04.500
Because up to now, a lot of it has been underground
and not very visible, we’re moving into

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:08.150
the very visible and exciting parts now.

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:11.920
The reconstruction of Courtenay Drive has
now been completed, and we really appreciate

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:15.860
the patience of nearby residents as this work
was carried out and we dealt with the discovery

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:20.439
of asbestos underneath the road surface.

00:01:20.439 --> 00:01:24.549
If you’ve been in the area over the last
few months, you will have noticed the cranes

00:01:24.549 --> 00:01:25.850
working away behind me.

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:31.569
Today we’re going get to get an update on
progress in the Kaiapoi Marine Precinct

00:01:31.569 --> 00:01:35.539
This is a large project which involves the
installation of a new river wall, the driving

00:01:35.539 --> 00:01:38.909
of new piles, and the complete reconstruction
of the stop bank.

00:01:38.909 --> 00:01:44.139
Lowering down the stopbank, is for Daniel
Smith to come back in and install the tie-backs,

00:01:44.139 --> 00:01:48.310
for the sheet-pile wall, which is pulling
on the tension for the new riverwall which

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:50.990
is going in.

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:55.850
Once that’s done, ECAN will come back to
reinstate the stop banks and once that’s

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:59.329
done, the builders for the terrace will come
back in and start building the terraces.

00:01:59.329 --> 00:02:03.560
It is hoped that the terraces will be completed
towards the end of this year, along with the

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:06.139
neighbouring private development.

00:02:06.139 --> 00:02:09.300
Installation of the floating pontoons will
require dredging of the river.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:10.300
Resource consent for that work has just been
consented, and it’s expected to take place

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:16.000
over winter as part of a wider dredging programme.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:20.670
A new draft Kaiapoi Town Centre plan will
soon be out for public consultation.

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:24.980
This document plans for the future of Kaiapoi’s
Town Centre and the adjacent Mixed-Use Business

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:25.980
Areas.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:28.780
Make sure you take a look at the plan and
submit your feedback when it’s released

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:31.540
in August.

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:36.260
In the next update, we’ll look at the soon-to-be
completed road link here in the Kaiapoi East

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:40.220
Regeneration Area which will be known as Feldwick
Drive, and we’ll talk about the upcoming

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:55.689
masterplan for this area including projects
like the dog park and bmx track.

